{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.signMixed_impossible_corpus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.signMixed_impossible_corpus","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L121-L127","doc":"**The corpus instance.**  For every colour parameter strictly inside\n`(-2, 2)` — the range in which the averaged interface is defined — the sign-mixed\npattern is unreachable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.corpusWeight_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.corpusWeight_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L118-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.corpusWeight_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.corpusWeight_pos","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L115-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.corpusWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.corpusWeight","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L110-L113","doc":"The corpus weight.  With colour parameter `delta` the pn offset is\n`d_pn = (1/2 + delta/4) * d_pp + (1/2 - delta/4) * d_nn`, so the weight is\n`w = 1/2 + delta/4`, strictly inside `(0,1)` exactly when `|delta| < 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.signMixed_impossible_of_combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.signMixed_impossible_of_combo","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L101-L108","doc":"**Corollary.**  No averaged pn letter can realise the sign-mixed pattern.\nThe hypothesis is exactly \"pn is a strict convex combination under an affine\ninterface law\"; the conclusion needs no numerical input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.signMixedPattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.signMixedPattern","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L96-L99","doc":"The required sign-mixed pattern, stated as `qou-q8vl` states it: the pn bond\nfactor exceeds one while both like-pair factors fall below it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.pn_not_strict_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.pn_not_strict_max","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**The exclusion.**  If the pn offset is a strict convex combination of the\nlike-pair offsets and the interface law is affine, then the pn bond factor\ncannot be the strict maximum of the three — so the sign-mixed pattern that\n`qou-q8vl` shows is required (pn above one, both like pairs below) is\nunreachable, for every `z`, every weight, and every offset pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.affine_preserves_combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.affine_preserves_combo","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The affine interface law `mu = z + d` carries a convex combination of\noffsets to the same convex combination of bond factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo_not_lt_both","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo_not_lt_both","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L65-L76","doc":"Symmetrically, it never falls strictly below both endpoints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo_not_gt_both","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo_not_gt_both","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L49-L63","doc":"A strict convex combination never strictly exceeds both of its endpoints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo_self","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L46-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.combo","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.lean#L41-L43","doc":"A strict convex combination of two values, with both weights strictly\npositive and summing to one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}